course: dictionary
lesson: 3962
title: Further: distance, more, and moving on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Further» can mean a greater distance. In «Buses keep to a timetable and don't wait, so that the people further along the route are not made late», further along means farther along the route, so those people are on a longer part of the journey. Ask yourself: is the word about how far, or how much?
explain: Further can also mean more or extra, as in «for further information». Here further does not mean distance at all. It means extra: you can find more details if you look at the place you are sent to.
explain: A whistle «can be heard much further away than a shout», so further is a comparison. The whistle reaches a greater distance than the shout. When you see further, look for a clue such as than, and then check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Further is the comparative of far, so it is used to compare two things.
fact: «Further» means at or to a greater distance, as in «further away».
fact: «Further» means more or extra, as in «further information».
fact: «To further something» means to help it move forward.
fact: Furthest is the form you use for the greatest distance of all.
exercise: «Buses keep to a timetable and don't wait, so that the people further along the route are not made late.» In this sentence, what does further mean? | Very quickly | *At a greater distance along the route | To help something move forward | More information
exercise: «A whistle can be heard much further away than a shout.» What does further compare here? | Loudness: the whistle is quieter | Time: the whistle lasts longer | Colour of the sound | *Distance: the whistle travels farther than the shout
exercise: «For further information, see page 10.» What does further mean? | Very far away in space | *More, or extra | To help something move forward | At a greater distance
test: Ann walked 5 km and Tom walked 3 km. Who walked further? | Tom | Nobody walked at all | They walked the same distance | *Ann
test: If a club helps your reading move forward, it will further your reading. Which meaning of further is this? | Later in time | *To help something move forward | More or extra | At a greater distance
exam: «Don't go any further» means what? | Return home | *Stop here | Walk faster | Go a long way
